# ==============================================================================
# The pinned Byakugan engine commit — the ONE place the engine version lives.
#
# The CAR lane (get_sybers_dxdfir.mitrecar) drives the Byakugan engine
# (https://github.com/Get-Sybers/byakugan) as an EXTERNAL recursive checkout:
# $BYAKUGAN_ROOT when set, else the `byakugan` directory next to (a sibling
# of) this repository. It is NOT a vendored submodule, so this file — not a
# gitlink — records the commit DX_DFIR is tested against. Everything that
# provisions or checks the engine reads it: scripts/setup-environment.sh
# (online hosts), scripts/package-offline.sh (the offline bundle),
# .github/workflows/smoke.yml (CI), and the python seam's off-pin warning.
#
# To bump the engine: edit the sha below to the new upstream commit, then
# re-provision — re-run scripts/setup-environment.sh, or manually:
#   git clone --recurse-submodules https://github.com/Get-Sybers/byakugan <root>
#   git -C <root> checkout <sha>
#   git -C <root> submodule update --init --recursive
# (recursive is REQUIRED: the engine reconstructs its object model live from
# its own nested car + attack-datasources submodules). A PR touching this file
# triggers the smoke workflow, which runs the real pipeline against the new pin.
#
# Format: readers take the FIRST non-comment, non-blank line as the ref. Keep
# it a full 40-hex sha — never a branch or tag — so checkouts are reproducible.
# ==============================================================================
0f02ab11ab08b6d8d5ce726f4779768442eb4b36
